[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-spray-application-decision :authorize-spray-application :proceed-with-spray-application :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007131-cloud-itonami-isco-7131-painters-and-related-workers-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the spray application" "finalize the spray application decision" "authorize the spray application" "authorize the spray-coating application" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799007132, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}", :actor/domain :production/spray-coating-shop-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:sprayer-verified :shop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7132", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007132: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7132 Spray Painters and Varnishers shop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7132\n-- Spray Painters and Varnishers** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of\nthe rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3 batches 1-4 already landed:\nconstruction/metal trades 7111-7222, agriculture 6113/6129/6223/6224/\n6310/6320).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7132\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/\nget-occupation \\\"7132\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Spray Painters and Varnishers\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7132` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7132` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nSpray painters and varnishers apply coatings using spray equipment --\nhigher physical-safety stakes than brush-painting (solvent/fume-\ninhalation exposure, flammable-material handling, ventilation/\nrespirator requirements). The controlling constraint for this vertical\nis that the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any op that\ndirectly finalizes a spray-application-execution decision, or\noverrides a shop safety officer's judgment -- those decisions must\nalways be a hard permanent block or an always-escalate op, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to SHOP\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs\nspray-painting work itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7131`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7131)\n(Painters and Related Workers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor`\nsplit, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same closely-related\ncoating-application safety pattern, already landed) -- cloned and read\nin full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7132` as an OSS shop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for spray painters and\nvarnishers, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Spray Shop\nAdvisor ⊣ SprayShopGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with\nan independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **shop scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct spray-application authority** -- it must NEVER be\ndesigned to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\nspray-application-execution decision, or any override of a shop safety\nofficer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind escalation --\nthey are structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a fume-exposure/ventilation/\n  flammability concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- paint/coating-materials procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nspray-application-execution decision or a shop-safety-officer-judgment\noverride. These are **structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-spray-application-decision` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names four\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`sprayshop.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-spray-application-decision`, `:authorize-spray-application`,\n`:proceed-with-spray-application`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`sprayshop.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-spray-application-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-spray-application`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-spray-application`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Sprayer unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered sprayer record (`:no-sprayer`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the sprayer is.\n2. **Shop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered spray shop (`:no-shop`). Together with check 1, this\n   directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a worker/shop\n   record must be independently verified/registered before any\n   action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the four\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with a spray\n   application, or overriding a shop safety officer's judgment, is a\n   second HARD, PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of the\n   allowlist check: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   spray-application-execution/safety-override language wherever it\n   appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a fume-exposure/\n  inadequate-ventilation/flammable-material observation -- it never\n  resolves the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is\n  the hazard data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about shop\n  safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  paint/coating-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  spray-application-execution or safety-officer-override attempt,\n  which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate\n  vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"spray\", \"coating\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nthis vertical's own vocabulary (a shop coordination actor working\nadjacent to spray-coating work necessarily discusses those concepts to\ndo its scheduling/logging job) could trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`sprayshop.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively as\nfinalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the spray\napplication\", \"authorize the spray application\", \"override the shop\nsafety officer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example\nphrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`sprayshop.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for sprayer ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\nspray-coating task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer review\")\nWITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-\nphrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this\nsession -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development. `sprayshop.actor-test/holds-a-scope-\nexcluded-op-even-at-high-confidence` additionally exercises the same\ninvariant through the full graph run, confirming a scope-excluded\nproposal never reaches `commit-record!` regardless of disposition\npath.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7132\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7132` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7132`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 21 tests, 45 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-spray-application` that is\n  merely gated behind an always-escalate list: rejected outright per\n  the task's explicit domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op\n  still means the *capability* to finalize a spray-application-\n  execution decision exists in the code path and is merely deferred to\n  a human gate. For a decision this severe (solvent/fume exposure,\n  flammable-material handling, inadequate ventilation), the capability\n  itself must not exist. The only op related to shop-safety escalation\n  is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for\n  human/shop-safety-officer attention and never itself decides,\n  authorizes, or defers a spray-application-execution decision for\n  later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block: rejected per the task's\n  explicit domain design -- an over-threshold paint/coating-materials\n  order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft escalate\n  gate, not a hard block; only the spray-application-execution/\n  safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"spray\" \"coating\"\n  \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses spray/\n  coating/safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so\n  a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale text that\n  deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Merging `sprayer` and `shop` into a single entity (only checking one\n  provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered sprayer AND independently-registered shop)\n  matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/shop record must be\n  independently verified/registered before any action\" and the\n  established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with\n  two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- task/materials-usage/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered sprayer AND\n   shop (`:no-sprayer`/`:no-shop`). Not a spray-application-execution\n   or safety-officer decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a spray-application-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   a specific spray-coating or spray-finish application -- it is a\n   calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a fume-exposure/inadequate-\n   ventilation/flammable-material concern to a human/shop safety\n   officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence\n   level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through\n   which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the shop safety\n   officer reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- paint/coating-materials\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a spray-application-\n   execution or authorization decision of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na spray-application-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a\nspecific spray-coating or spray-finish application) or a shop-safety-\nofficer-judgment override -- these categories are structurally absent,\nnot gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`sprayshop.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) four concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit level\n(`sprayshop.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`sprayshop.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-spray-application-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-spray-application`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-spray-application`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`sprayshop.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a spray application or override a shop\nsafety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`sprayshop.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 21, :assertions 45, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Spray Coating Shop Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :sprayer-verification :shop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7132", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7132", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7132], :test/simulator :sprayshop.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7132 — Spray Painters and Varnishers Shop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7132}]